prompt:
Use case: precise-object-edit
Asset type: transparent production accessory atlas derived from an already fitted wardrobe
Image 1 is the selected four-view moon-post worn outfit. Image 2 is its cape-only wear master, which reveals cloth hidden by the bag. Image 3 is the corrected star-collar wear master. Extract and finish the SAME six accessories as reusable standalone images; preserve their colours, shapes, soft broad folds, warm dark-brown line weight, sparse motifs and design. Do not design a new wardrobe.
Layout: exactly 4 columns and 6 rows, generous empty transparent gutters. Columns always FRONT, THREE-QUARTER RIGHT, PROFILE RIGHT, BACK. Rows always:
1 lavender crescent beret;
2 narrow lavender neck ribbon with cream five-point star charm and two short cream ribbon ends (back shows only rear ribbon);
3 short lavender star cape with raised collar, tiny clasp and open front from Image 2; fill only the cloth previously hidden by hands or bag;
4 rounded cream envelope satchel with pink seal and believable complete shoulder strap; back shows its back/flap appropriately, never an extra hand;
5 shallow constellation arc of exactly three small cream/gold stars connected by a thin muted lavender arc;
6 a PAIR of soft lavender crescent ankle boots, TWO boots in each cell, side by side with a transparent gap. Both point consistently with that cell's character-facing direction. Profile includes one complete near and one complete far boot, not chopped halves. Back boots show heels, no front crescent on heel.
These are detachable production items after a worn-first design, not a concept collage. Remove all character bodies, faces, ears, hands, feet, tails and scenery. Reconstruct garment areas that were occluded, but keep original visible design unchanged. Every cell contains only its one accessory, or the one two-boot pair. Keep comparable sizes across views within a row. Leave every silhouette complete and separate from neighbouring cells.
Smooth hand-drawn line art with restrained gentle material shading. Not pixel art, not coarse blocks, not photoreal, no dense fabric stitch patterns or shiny metal. True transparent alpha, no background/floor/shadows, no baked checkerboard. NO text, labels, arrows, panel borders or decorative extra elements.
